```rust
fn bubble_sort<T: PartialOrd>(array: &[T]) {
    let mut i: usize = 0;
    let mut j: usize = array.len() - 1;

    while j >= i {
        if array[j] < array[j - 1] {
            let temp = array[j];
            array[j] = array[j - 1];
            array[j - 1] = temp;

            i = j;
            j -= 1;
        } else {
            j -= 1;
        }
    }
}
```
This function takes a slice of elements as its parameter and sorts it in ascending order using the bubble sort algorithm. The algorithm works by repeatedly swapping adjacent elements if they are in the wrong order, until the elements are sorted. The `PartialOrd` trait is used to specify that the elements can be partially ordered, which is necessary for the algorithm to work correctly.

