You can run a command on a remote server through SSH using the Node.js child_process.execFile() method.

For example:
```js
const execFile = require('child_process').execFile;

execFile('ssh', ['user@host', 'ls'], (error, stdout, stderr) => {
  if (error) {
    console.error(error);
  }
  console.log(stdout);
});
```

This will:

- Use the ssh command to connect to the host as the user 
- Run the ls command to list files
- The stdout will contain the result
- stderr will contain any errors

You can run any shell command on the remote host this way.

The full syntax is:
```js
execFile(file [,args][, options][, callback])
```

So you'd pass 'ssh' as the file, the host and command as args, and a callback to get the response.

