The bubble sort algorithm is a simple sorting algorithm that sorts a list of numbers in ascending or descending order by repeatedly comparing adjacent elements and swaping them if they are in order.

Here's the bubble sort algorithm in JavaScript:
```javascript
function bubbleSort(arr) {
  const n = arr.length;
  for (let i = 0; i < n; i++) {
    for (let j = 0; j < n-i-1; j++) {
      if (arr[j] > arr[j+1]) {
        const temp = arr[j];
        arr[j] = arr[j+1];
        arr[j+1] = temp;
      }
    }
  }
  return arr;
}
```
This function takes a list of numbers as an input and sorts it in descending order. The function uses two nested loops to compare adjacent elements and swap them if they are in order. The outer loop iterates `n-i-1` times, where `i` is the current index of the outer loop and `n` is the length of the input list. The inner loop iterates `i` times, where `j` is the current index of the inner loop and `n-i-1` is the size of the input list.

The function returns the sorted list of numbers.

