Migrating from Bootstrap to MUI (Material UI) involves replacing Bootstrap components with equivalent MUI components. Here are some steps to migrate:

1. Install MUI. Run `npm install @material-ui/core` or `yarn add @material-ui/core`.

2. Replace Bootstrap's grid system with MUI's grid. MUI's grid works very similarly, you just use `<Grid>` elements instead of `<Row>` and `<Col>`.

3. Replace Bootstrap buttons with MUI buttons. Use `<Button>` instead of `<Button>` and pass a `variant` prop to specify button type (`contained`, `outlined`, `text`).

4. Replace Bootstrap forms with MUI forms. Use `<TextField>` instead of `<FormControl>` and `<Input>`. Use `<FormLabel>`, `<RadioGroup>`, `<FormControlLabel>` for labels and radio buttons.

5. Replace Bootstrap cards with MUI cards. Use `<Card>` and `<CardContent>` instead of `<Card>` and `<CardBody>`.

6. Replace Bootstrap navs with MUI tabs or bottom navigation. Use `<Tabs>` and `<Tab>` for tabbed navigation, `<BottomNavigation>` and `<BottomNavigationAction>` for bottom nav.

7. Use MUI icons instead of Bootstrap icons. MUI has its own `@material-ui/icons` package with 1000+ icons.

8. Customize the MUI theme for Bootstrap-like styling. You can make MUI look more like Bootstrap by overriding default theme values:

```js
import { createMuiTheme } from '@material-ui/core/styles';

