1. Install the `react-native-oauth2-client` library:
```java
npm install react-native-oauth2-client
```
2. Configure the library with your app's information, including the client ID, client secret, and redirect URI:
```php
import OAuth2Client from 'react-native-oauth2-client';

const clientId = 'your-client-id';
const clientSecret = 'your-client-secret';
const redirectUri = 'your-app-redirect-uri';

const oauth2Client = new OAuth2Client(clientId, clientSecret, redirectUri);
```
3. Use the `oauth2Client.getAccessToken()` method to obtain an access token by sending a request to the authorization server with the appropriate grant type (e.g., authorization code or implicit) and scope:
```javascript
const tokenRequest = await oauth2Client.getAccessToken({
  grant_type: 'authorization_code',
  code: 'your-authorization-code',
  redirect_uri: 'your-app-redirect-uri',
  scope: 'openid email profile',
});
```
4. Use the obtained access token to make API requests to protected resources:
```javascript
const response = await fetch('https://your-api-endpoint.com/protected-resource', {
  headers: {
    Authorization: `Bearer ${tokenRequest.access_token}`,
  },
});
```
5. When the access token expires, use the `oauth2Client.getRefreshToken()` method to obtain a refresh token and obtain a new access token:
```javascript
const refreshRequest = await oauth2Client.getRefreshToken(tokenRequest.refresh_token);
const refreshToken = refreshRequest.refresh_token;

const newAccessTokenRequest = await oauth2Client.getAccessToken({
