var_dump($NAME_1);
```
This implementation uses a nested `for` loop to iterate through the elements and swap them if they are in the wrong order. The outer `while` loop ensures that the sorting continues until no more swaps are needed. The `n` parameter determines the number of elements to be sorted (the subarray size). By default, it is set to 1, which means the entire array will be sorted.

