Here's an example of a simple C program that takes BTRFS snapshots daily:

1.   First, we need to include the BTRFS file system header:


```c
#include <btrfs/btrfs.h>

```

1.   Next, we need to create a BTRFS superblock:


```c
struct btrfs_super_block *super = btrfs_alloc_super();

```

1.   Initialize super block with default parameters:


```c
btrfs_set_default_params(super);

```

1.   Calculate the total size of the snapshot:


```c
btrfs_get_capacity(super->fs_info, &total_size);

```

1.   Allocate a chunk of memory for the snapshot data:


```c
struct btrfs_dev_id devid;
devid.name = "snapshot-data";
devid.uuid = btrfs_alloc_uuid();
struct btrfs_fs_info *fsinfo = super->fs_info;
fsinfo->dev_id = &devid;
fsinfo->fsid = 0;
fsinfo->chunk_size = BTRFS_CHUNK_SIZE;
fsinfo->data_size = total_size;
fsinfo->data_type = BTRFS_DATA_REPEAT;
fsinfo->log_size = total_size * 2;
fsinfo->num_stripes = 2;
fsinfo->stripes[0].size = total_size - (total_size * 2);
fsinfo->stripes[1].size = total_size * 2;

```

1.   Create the snapshot:


```c
btrfs_create_snapshot(super, &devid);

```

1.   Create the snapshot data:


```c
struct btrfs_file *file = btrfs_alloc_file(fsinfo->data_size);
file->generation = 0;
file->type = BTRFS_FILE_TYPE_DATA;
file->mode = BTRFS_FILE_MODE_DATA;
btrfs_map_file(file);
btrfs_commit_file(file);
btrfs_free_file(file);

```

1.   Add the snapshot data to the file system:


```c
btrfs_file_info_add(file, 0, total_size * 2, total_size, fsinfo->fsid);

```

1.   Close the snapshot:


```c
btrfs_create_snapshot(super, &devid, false);

```

1.   Restore the snapshot:


```c
btrfs_restore_snapshot(super, &devid);

```

This is just a simple example and there are many ways to extend it to suit your needs, such as compressing the snapshot data before taking the snapshot, starting the snapshot at a specific time, or updating the snapshot data continuously.

