To select multiple cells in an Angular PrimeNG table and change their values at once, you can use the following steps:

1. Import the necessary modules in your Angular component:
```typescript
import { Component, EventEmitter } from '@angular/core';
import { TableModule, Table, TableRow, TableCell } from 'primeng/table';
```
2. In your component's template, add the following code to create the table:
```php
<table [mdbTable]="table" [mdbRowData]="rows" [mdbColumnDefs]="columnDefs">
  <tr>
    <th mdb-column-header (click)="toggleSelect()">
      Select
    </th>
  </tr>
  <tr *ngFor="let row of rows">
    <td mdb-column-body [mdbTableCell]="cell"
        [mdbFormGroupName]="selected"
        [mdbSelect]="selected === cell"
        (ngSubmit)="updateSelectedValue()">
      {{cell.value}}
    </td>
  </tr>
</table>
```
3. Define the `columnDefs` property in your component's class to specify the column definitions for the table:
```kotlin
columnDefs = [
  { field: 'name', headerName: 'Name' },
  { field: 'age', headerName: 'Age' },
];
```
4. Create an array of objects to represent the rows in the table:
```css
rows = [
  { name: 'NAME_1 NAME_2', age: 30 },
  { name: 'NAME_3', age: 25 },
  { name: 'NAME_4 NAME_5', age: 40 },
];
```
5. Define the `selected` property to store the selected values:
```css
selected = { name: '', age: '' };
```
6. Define the `toggleSelect()` method to toggle the selection of a cell:
```javascript
toggleSelect() {
  const selected = this.table.getSelectedData();
  if (selected.length > 0) {
    this.table.deselectAll();
  } else {
    this.table.selectAll();
  }
}

