Yes, you can partition an array in JavaScript using a predicate callback function. The basic approach is to iterate through the array, and for each element, apply the predicate function to determine which subarray it should belong to. Then, push the element onto the appropriate subarray. Here's an example implementation:
```scss
function partition(array, predicate) {
  const result = [];
  let left = [];
  let right = [];

  for (let i = 0; i < array.length; i++) {
    const element = array[i];
    if (predicate(element)) {
      right.push(element);
    } else {
      left.push(element);
    }
  }

  result.push(...left, ...right);
  return result;
}
```
