```glsl
#version 330

uniform sampler2D image; // the image to be blurred

void main()
{
    // the blur offset
    float offset = 1.0 / (texture(image, ivec2(gl_FragCoord.xy)).r + 1.0);

    // get the color and alpha components
    vec3 color = texture(image, ivec2(gl_FragCoord.xy)).rgb;
    float alpha = texture(image, ivec2(gl_FragCoord.xy)).a;

    // invert the colors
    color.rgb = vec3(1.0 - color.r, 1.0 - color.g, 1.0 - color.b);
    alpha = 1.0 - alpha;

    // set the output color
    gl_FragColor = vec4(color, alpha);
}
```
This shader uses the texture lookup function `texture(image, ivec2(gl_FragCoord.xy))` to sample the color and alpha components of the image at the current fragment's coordinates. It then uses these values to calculate an offset, which is used to blur the image. The fragment shader then inverts the colors by multiplying the RGB components by (1 - R), (1 - G), and (1 - B) respectively, and multiplying the alpha component by (1 - A). Finally, it sets the output color to the blurred color and alpha.

