Here is a C# function that will increment or decrement between two gear numbers:

```csharp
void ShiftGears(int currentGear, int nextGear)
{
    if (currentGear < nextGear)
    {
        // Increment gears
        for (int i = currentGear; i <= nextGear; i++)
        {
            Console.WriteLine("Shifting to gear " + i);
        }
    }
    else
    {
        // Decrement gears
        for (int i = currentGear; i >= nextGear; i--)
        {
            Console.WriteLine("Shifting to gear " + i);
        }
    }
}
```

This function will:

- Check if the currentGear is less than nextGear. If so, increment the gears. 
- Otherwise, decrement the gears. 
- It will print each gear shift using a for loop.

So you could call it like this:
```csharp
ShiftGears(3, 5);  // Increment from 3 to 5
ShiftGears(5, 3);  // Decrement from 5 to 3
```

And it would print:
