Here's a JavaScript code snippet to output the first ten elements of the Fibonacci sequence in random order:
```javascript
function generateRandomFibonacci() {
  const maxIndex = 9;
  const lowestIndex = 0;
  const fibonacciSequence = [0, 1];

  for (let i = lowestIndex; i < maxIndex; i++) {
    const next = fibonacciSequence[i] + fibonacciSequence[i + 1];
    fibonacciSequence.push(next);
  }

  const shuffledSequence = [...fibonacciSequence].sort(() => Math.random() - 0.5);
  return shuffledSequence.slice(0, 10);
}

console.log(generateRandomFibonacci());
```
This code first generates the Fibonacci sequence up to the 10th element (index 9) and then shuffles the sequence using the Fisher-Yates shuffle algorithm. Finally, it slices the shuffled sequence to get the first 10 elements.

