1. Use the browser's developer tools: Most modern browsers come with built-in developer tools that can help you profile your JavaScript code. For example, in Chrome, you can open the DevTools panel by right-clicking on the page and selecting "Inspect". Once the panel is open, you can select the "Profiles" tab and click the "Record Profile" button to start a profile. You can then interact with your page and the profile will show you a breakdown of how long each function took to execute.
