For example, consider the following outer loop:
```java
for (int i = 0; i < 5; i++) {
    for (int j = 0; j < 2 * i; j++) {
        // code to be executed
    }
}
```
In this example, the outer loop iterates 5 times, and the inner loop iterates 2 times the number of times the outer loop iterates. Therefore, the inner loop will iterate 2 \* 5 = 10 times.

