* `condition`: This is an expression that is evaluated before each iteration of the loop. If the condition is true, the loop body is executed. For example, `i < 10` is a condition that will be true as long as `i` is less than 10.
* `increment/decrement`: This is an expression that is evaluated at the end of each iteration of the loop. It is used to update the loop control variable. For example, `i++` increments the variable `i` by 1.
* `{ ... }`: This is the code that is executed repeatedly by the loop.

