3. Access your server through a proxy. Set up a proxy server that has CORS enabled, and have it proxy requests to your Socket.IO server.

4. Use JSONP instead of CORS. Socket.IO supports JSONP transport which works around CORS.

5. Host your client and server on the same origin (domain/port). If they have the same origin, CORS is not needed.

