SPL (System Parameter Loader) is a bootloader that initializes the Linux kernel and other components of the Linux operating system. It is typically stored on non-volatile memory such as NAND flash.

The reason why you need to write SPL to NAND flash using imx-kobs in Linux is that U-Boot is not capable of writing to NAND flash directly. U-Boot is a bootloader that is designed to boot other operating systems, but it does not have the capabilities to write to NAND flash.

