1. Use constexpr for constants like MAXN, dx, dy, NAME_2. This indicates to the compiler that these values are constant and can be optimized accordingly.

2. Use std::vector<std::string> instead of std::vector<std::vector<char>> for the world map. This is a more natural representation for a 2D string array.

3. Use uint16_t for N and M instead of int16_t. Since the maximum value is 1000, uint16_t is sufficient and more appropriate as an unsigned type.

4. Initialize prevX, prevY to -1 instead of 1e9. This is a more natural "invalid" value for coordinates.

5. Use std::string for the path instead of building it character by character. This is more efficient.

