We also define two functions `isEven` and `isOdd` that take an `Int` as input and return a `Boolean` indicating whether the number is even or odd, respectively.

In the `main` function, we create two instances of the `Predicate` interface, `evenPredicate` and `oddPredicate`, that represent the conditions for selecting even and odd numbers, respectively.

We then use the `filter` method of the collection to filter the numbers based on the `Predicate` instances. The resulting lists of even and odd numbers are printed to the console.

This is just a basic example of how to implement the Predicate design pattern in Kotlin, but you can use it in many other ways depending on your specific use case.

