const buttonClick = debounce(() => {
  // handle button click
}, 1000);

button.addEventListener('click', buttonClick);

```

This code adds a click event listener to a button with an ID of "myButton", and debounces the click event for 1 second (1000 milliseconds). When the button is clicked again, the debounced function will be called, allowing the button to be clicked again immediately without any delay.

