=================================================================================

ECMAScript Modules (ESM) are a new feature introduced in ECMAScript 6 that allow you to write modular JavaScript code. They offer several benefits over traditional module systems, such as the ability to use the `import` and `export` keywords to import and export values between modules.

To use ESM in your Node.js project, you'll need to configure your npm package to support it. Here's how to do it:

Prerequisites
-------------

