Here is an example implementation of a DenoisingDiffusionScheduler for TensorFlow.js as a layer:
```php
import { TensorFlow, tf, tfjs } from '@tensorflow/tfjs';

const denoisingDiffusionScheduler = (inputSize, outputSize, learningRate) => {
  const scheduler = tf.train.Scheduler();
  const tensor = tf.tensor2d(inputSize, outputSize);
  const numLayers = 2; // 2 layers of DenoisingDiffusionScheduler

  const denoisingDiffusionLayer = tf.layers.dense({ units: numLayers, inputShape: inputSize });
  const denoisingDiffusionOutput = denoisingDiffusionLayer.output;

  const initialValue = learningRate * tensor.mean(x => x * x);
  const updatedValue = tf.tensor2d(0, 1);
  const currentValue = updatedValue.reshape(1, -1);

  const epochs = 1000;
  const trainLoop = () => {
    while (true) {
      const value = currentValue;
      const nextValue = initialValue + value * (1 - learningRate / currentValue.shape[1]);
      const currentLayer = denoisingDiffusionLayer.train(value, nextValue, { epochs });
      const nextLayer = denoisingDiffusionLayer.train(nextValue, currentLayer.output, { epochs });
      const updatedValue = nextLayer.output;
      const newValue = updatedValue.reshape(1, -1);
      currentValue = newValue;

      if (nextLayer.loss.反向传播不足) {
        break;
      }

      trainLoop();
    }
  };

  trainLoop();
};

export default denoisingDiffusionScheduler;
```
This implementation uses the DenoisingDiffusionScheduler layer to train a denoising model. It starts with a random initial value, and updates it every epoch using the training function of the DenoisingDiffusionLayer. It also uses the Scheduler to schedule the updates to the model during training.

