2. There was a network interruption that caused the connection to drop.

3. The server deliberately closed the connection due to timeout or some other policy.

4. There was an issue with the firewall, proxy or load balancer that caused the connection to be dropped.

To handle this exception, you should:

1. Catch the IOException and handle it gracefully. You can retry the request or reconnect as needed.

2. Check your network connectivity and firewall settings. Make sure there are no issues.

3. Check with the server/service owner to see if there are any known issues.

4. You may need to build in some retry logic and timeout handling in your application in case of such transient network errors.

