Here's a JavaScript function that extracts the first year of the financials from the given string:
```javascript
function extractFinancialsYear(str) {
  const financialsStart = str.indexOf("Financials");
  const financialsEnd = str.indexOf("\n\n", financialsStart);
  const financials = str.substring(financialsStart, financialsEnd);

  const salesStart = financials.indexOf("Sales ");
  const salesEnd = financials.indexOf("\n", salesStart);
  const sales = financials.substring(salesStart, salesEnd);

  const regex = /(\d{4})/;
  const match = regex.exec(sales);
  return match[1];
}
```
