Absolutely! Here's a generic solution for invoking all handlers of a multicast delegate concurrently:

```csharp
public static Task[] InvokeAll<T>(this MulticastDelegate multicastDelegate, Func<Delegate, object[], Task> invocationFunc) 
    where T : MulticastDelegate
{
    if (multicastDelegate == null) return Array.Empty<Task>();
    var delegates = multicastDelegate.GetInvocationList().Cast<T>();
    var tasks = new Task[delegates.Count()];
    for (int i = 0; i < delegates.Count(); i++) 
    {
        tasks[i] = invocationFunc(delegates.ElementAt(i), multicastDelegate.GetInvocationList());
    }
    return tasks;
}
```

